{"timestamp": "2026-08-14T11:31:06.492452+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:fb41758b35af", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson fb41758b35af via .agent/tools/learn.py: \"When a bash script under test resolves its own location via ${BASH_SOURCE[0]}/SCRIPT_DIR for self-referential logic (e.g. 'am I the canonical checkout'), a pytest fixture that spoofs cwd while invoking the real, on-disk script file does NOT exercise the 'invoked from a different checkout' scenario \u2014 SCRIPT_DIR always resolves to where the file physically lives, regardless of subprocess cwd. To test that logic in isolation, copy the actual script (plus its sourced dependencies) into the synthetic fixture directory and invoke that copy.\"", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_fb4175"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-08-14T11:31:06.492452+00:00"]}
