{"timestamp": "2026-08-14T13:55:50.027169+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:ecf446018e17", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson ecf446018e17 via .agent/tools/learn.py: \"When a script compares 'sibling repositories' by directory path, a linked git worktree of the SAME canonical repo is not a downstream mirror target \u2014 it's an alternate checkout of the identical guard authority. Distinguish them via 'git -C <root> rev-parse --git-common-dir' (resolved to an absolute path): if two roots share the same common dir, they're worktrees of one repo, not independent siblings, and should be skipped rather than scanned for divergence.\"", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_ecf446"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-08-14T13:55:50.027169+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-14T13:55:50.465945+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:e6771ac33caa", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson e6771ac33caa via .agent/tools/learn.py: \"A script that runs 'git -C <other-repo>' against multiple repositories, when itself invoked as a git hook (or from within a hook's call chain), must clear git's own local-environment variables first -- 'unset' every name from 'git rev-parse --local-env-vars' (GIT_DIR, GIT_WORK_TREE, GIT_INDEX_FILE, etc.) before the first cross-repo git call. Hooks export these for their OWN repo context; left set, they silently rebind every subsequent '-C <other-repo>' call back to the invoking repo instead of the target.\"", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_e6771a"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-08-14T13:55:50.465945+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-14T13:56:05.275577+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:f5a3139114c2", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson f5a3139114c2 via .agent/tools/learn.py: \"When multiple agent sessions work the same infrastructure-critical fix concurrently (guard scripts, pre-push hooks, canonical-repo tooling), a shared append-only coordination board (this repo's GossipBus, queried via orchestrator.coordination.paths.canonical_db_path()) is what prevented duplicate/conflicting work across at least 4 concurrent agents on this single fix. The pattern that worked: post status BEFORE and AFTER any consequential step (not just at the end), read the board fresh before deciding next action rather than trusting your own last-known state, and treat the latest timestamped ruling as authoritative even when it contradicts an earlier instruction in the same thread -- rulings evolve as agents verify things live.\"", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_f5a313"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-08-14T13:56:05.275577+00:00"]}
