{"timestamp": "2026-08-15T00:16:55.272880+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:c06864656734", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson c06864656734 via .agent/tools/learn.py: \"When consolidating append-only JSONL memory files across branches, never use naive bash tools like 'sort -u' or key-based JSON deduplication, which can mangle text or drop legacy schema entries. Instead, perform a strict, lossless string-level union against the untouched canonical base (e.g. origin/main) in an isolated staging area to ensure zero data loss.\"", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_c06864"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-08-15T00:16:55.272880+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-16T09:43:30.506943+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:5639c5f22ce9", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 5639c5f22ce9 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'When git push fails with authentication or invalid password errors on macOS due to a conflicting exported GITHUB_TOKEN environment variable, run: env -u GITHUB_TOKEN gh auth setup-git && env -u GITHUB_TOKEN git push --force-with-lease origin <branch>. Unsetting GITHUB_TOKEN forces git to use valid macOS Keychain / gh CLI credentials while --force-with-lease prevents overwriting unexpected remote commits.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_5639c5"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-08-16T09:43:30.506943+00:00"]}
