{"timestamp": "2026-09-12T10:14:41.494043+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:2d3ced9f9317", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 2d3ced9f9317 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'When chunking Base64-encoded content for a multi-part API write, the chunk size must be a multiple of 3 raw bytes (e.g. 12288 = 4096x3); any other size makes an interior chunk end in Base64 padding, and a standards-conformant decoder treats padding as end-of-stream, silently truncating everything concatenated after it with no error at any step'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_2d3ced"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-12T10:14:41.494043+00:00"]}
