{"timestamp":"2026-08-05T21:06:45.948715+00:00","skill":"cross-repo-coordination-week","action":"weekly-retrospective-2026-07-30-to-2026-08-06","result":"success","detail":"success","pain_score":5,"importance":9,"reflection":"OBSERVATION (past ~7 days + 2026-08-06): PT/orama multi-agent week spanned (1) stale-branch rehabilitation and history-boundary discipline on episodic memory branches, (2) security F1â€“F9 / guard-sync + PR-body HMAC grant landing (PT #320 pairing orama), (3) CodeRabbit remediation waves including PT #98 lineage follow-through and later cloud-start/guard PRs, (4) PT dream/review-queue cycles with AGENTS.md as memory authority (tools-only LESSONS.md; no hand edits), (5) JobSpec/TaskEnvelope absorption history culminating in Hermes T-ENG-1 + Waves 1â€“2 JSON-envelope reconciliation on orama (four incompatible shapes mapped to hermes-universal-invocation-protocol.md; Appendix C platform gaps deferred v2.1++), (6) Relay Cursor registration/handoff on PT WORKSPACE while Codex owned Hermes reconciliation recall (e0e9ea24), (7) coordination via agent_coordination board + GossipBus claim patterns, (8) Codex ownership boundary respected for memory commits vs concurrent workspace notes, (9) provenance/identity rules (no fabricated agent identities; no forbidden co-authors on new commits; inspect before stage), (10) local-only safeguards kept devices.yml/models.yml/vendor/ecc-tools intentionally dirty and unpushed.\n\nINFERENCE (not motive diagnosis): concurrent branch/worktree density plus stale docs/branch ambiguity repeatedly caused agents to treat orphaned tips as unmerged work; dual-voice review helped, but duplicated PRs and cross-agent commit attribution friction remain when there is no single live board/claim protocol. Deep memory helps recall doctrine across harnesses but does not substitute for HITL gates when agents overstep (scope creep, PR-body clobber history, autonomous pushes).\n\nHUMAN OPERATOR â€” strengths (evidence-based): sequences le