{"timestamp": "2026-09-17T02:33:06.841361+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:19af935a717c", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 19af935a717c via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'OSSF normative drafts live in orama-system PR #360 docs/v2/references/ as an informative mirror; OpenClaw references/ remains the pre-ratification working tree \u2014 construction guide and reconciliation plan are hub-only unless explicitly copied to the orama mirror'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_19af93"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-17T02:33:06.841361+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-17T02:44:32.765809+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:2a1bbf67f23d", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 2a1bbf67f23d via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Before pushing to a shared PR branch, git fetch and diff origin/<branch>..HEAD first -- another agent can commit directly into the same physical worktree path across sessions with no board signal until a later digest post, so a local HEAD commit is provisional until verified against the remote tip, not assumed to be yours alone.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_2a1bbf"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-17T02:44:32.765809+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-17T02:44:39.656721+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:c5d8128b119e", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson c5d8128b119e via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'When mirroring a document set into a different co-located target directory, path prefixes get deliberately re-normalized for the new context (e.g. references/foo.md becomes foo.md once siblings are co-located in the mirror) -- never blindly copy lint or content fixes back to the canonical source without checking whether a given diff line is a deliberate context-specific normalization or a real defect.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_c5d812"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-17T02:44:39.656721+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-17T02:44:47.005900+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:6eb0e9c56288", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 6eb0e9c56288 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'A document that has lived for weeks in a non-git-tracked private folder has never been checked by any linter the target repo enforces -- expect real, pre-existing markdownlint/hygiene debt on first mirror into a CI-gated repo, not just the new content added during the mirror itself; run the actual linter, not a visual read, before treating a long-lived draft as CI-ready.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_6eb0e9"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-17T02:44:47.005900+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-19T02:06:45.032446+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:b7d7be187d74", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson b7d7be187d74 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'For a security PR that must be reconciled from a limited sandbox, preserve every remote tip with an immutable backup ref; work in a clean linked worktree from the verified head; simulate and resolve conflicts additively; verify the exact resulting tree and parent chain; publish only a normal fast-forward update (never force); then re-fetch the remote head and compare the intended tree before reporting. For cross-repository endpoint-policy stacks, declare the exact peer ref rather than assuming equal branch names or silently falling back to main.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_b7d7be"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-19T02:06:45.032446+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-19T08:20:58.097187+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:5bec3440ef6b", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 5bec3440ef6b via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'When a GitHub Actions resolve step writes GITHUB_OUTPUT via echo inside double quotes that also backslash-quotes GITHUB_HEAD_REF, the sibling-ref resolver receives literal quote characters, misses the stack-map key, and same-named-ref fallback checks out the PT branch name on the peer repo. Diagnose from the checkout fetch refspec in the job log (quoted refs/heads fragments), not from continue-on-error conclusion=success. Write GITHUB_OUTPUT from a --github-output helper; log the input head and resolved peer; checkout the open sibling PR branch until that PR is merged into main, then use main; if a declared peer checkout fails, fail the job instead of silently falling back to main and greenwashing cross-repo parity.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_5bec34"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-19T08:20:58.097187+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-19T09:41:27.323925+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:bb6bb14284a5", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson bb6bb14284a5 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'PT #395 went green at 8cc496b after three real failures, not because 7f8b834 looked checked: (1) quoted echo of GITHUB_HEAD_REF into GITHUB_OUTPUT made stack-map lookup miss, checkout used the PT branch name on orama-system, continue-on-error fell through to orama main, and endpoint-policy parity compared the wrong tree -- write GITHUB_OUTPUT via --github-output, checkout the open Orama PR 363 branch cursor/tiered-pipeline-runtime-fb76 until that PR merges then use main, and fail declared-peer checkout instead of silent main fallback; diagnose from the job-log fetch refspec, not conclusion=success. (2) Remote orama_bridge Bearer hops need an HTTPS url_checker on every redirect, and packaged endpoint_policy hosts must not treat startswith 127-dot as loopback. (3) Memory-gate tests mint sha256(claim) while learn.py mints cluster.pattern_id(claim, conditions); the hook must accept both tooling mints and still reject invented ids. A SHA with zero Actions runs is not CI green even if CodeRabbit is success.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_bb6bb1"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-19T09:41:27.323925+00:00"]}
