{"timestamp": "2026-09-26T03:37:24.904282+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:886258809448", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 886258809448 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'git diff --cached is the right pre-commit default and is empty on a CI checkout. CI must pass an explicit three-dot base and head. For pull requests use the pull-request head SHA, not the synthetic merge commit.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_886258"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-26T03:37:24.904282+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-26T03:37:25.071965+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:793c8a605f43", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 793c8a605f43 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Lockstep copies of the prohibited-address scanner must match including docstrings. Perpetua-Tools implements it in scripts/review/repo_hygiene_core.py. orama-system keeps a monolith scripts/review/repo_hygiene.py with no core module, and its tests exempt that monolith path.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_793c8a"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-26T03:37:25.071965+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-26T03:37:25.212424+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:4ed523cc3d15", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 4ed523cc3d15 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Resolving a GitHub review thread does not change the parent review state, which stays COMMENTED. Reply on the inline discussion with the full forty-character fixing commit SHA, then resolve the thread. An outdated comment has a null line and still needs that reply.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_4ed523"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-26T03:37:25.212424+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-26T03:37:25.359778+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:392f8817a393", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 392f8817a393 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'While syncing a hygiene gate across repos, do not commit unrelated local edits to identity policy or cursor PR-body scripts. Dropping an allowed automation identity from a repo bot-identity list is a policy regression, not part of the gate.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_392f88"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-26T03:37:25.359778+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-26T03:37:25.498522+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:ef546c0b6d79", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson ef546c0b6d79 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Full narrative for the 2026-09-26 staged private-range gate on Perpetua-Tools PR 399 and orama-system PR 366 is at .agent/memory/working/2026-09-26-staged-private-range-gate-pt399-orama366.md'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_ef546c"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-26T03:37:25.498522+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-26T05:35:38.320678+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:b4b39bd86ecd", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson b4b39bd86ecd via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'When a Cursor cloud worker must coordinate with a Mac-local GossipBus, treat the SQLite board as intra-host only: cloud VMs cannot claim the local queue atomically. Use PR comments plus a local handoff file for remote visibility; on same-machine summons, emit via GossipBus and always pair agent_note with agent_pulse.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_b4b39b"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-26T05:35:38.320678+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-26T05:35:38.556990+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:a17856504b2a", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson a17856504b2a via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'A GossipBus review job whose notes say do not claim until a published source_ref and expected_base_sha exist must stay held even when depends_on is empty. Empty depends_on is not permission to claim.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_a17856"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-26T05:35:38.556990+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-26T05:35:38.777432+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:ec064e8b08df", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson ec064e8b08df via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'For Kungfu Wave 0 local drafts, treat Python manifest validation as the fail-closed authority and JSON Schema as shape-only until schema encodes ownership routing. A green pytest suite that never opens sources/v1-skill-manifest.jsonl does not prove the inventory is safe.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_ec064e"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-26T05:35:38.777432+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-26T05:35:39.003049+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:a8a799f105d2", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson a8a799f105d2 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'After merging a lockstep PT and orama hygiene pair, post the full session closeout and graduated lesson table as a PR comment on the merged PT PR rather than rewriting the PR body under strict body-guard mode.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_a8a799"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-26T05:35:39.003049+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-26T05:35:39.246907+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:7e8df60c294f", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 7e8df60c294f via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Refresh the local coordination handoff registry and board snapshot after consequential board writes so a remotely summoned worker sees current merge tips and open holds.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_7e8df6"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-26T05:35:39.246907+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-26T05:36:10.659874+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:a926b2bf36bc", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson a926b2bf36bc via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Full narrative for the 2026-09-26 PT#399/orama#366 post-merge session follow-up (remote worker, Kungfu W0 reviews, PR-comment closeout) is at .agent/memory/working/2026-09-26-pt399-orama366-session-followup-lessons.md'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_a926b2"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-26T05:36:10.659874+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-25T15:45:11.895066+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:0c7355deb939", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 0c7355deb939 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'A bash script that runs set -u must length-guard EVERY array expansion, because macOS stock bash 3.2 treats an empty-array expansion of the form dollar-brace-arr-at-brace as an unbound-variable error rather than an empty expansion. Canonical idiom: [[ ${#arr[@]} -gt 0 ]] && cmd+=(arr-elements). This is the THIRD recurrence of the same defect class (after commit_clean_test.sh verify_args and a profiling wrapper), so treat it as a systemic pattern: when fixing one instance, scan every set -u script in the repo with a single regex for unguarded += expansions and fix all confirmed instances, then prove the fix against a stubbed dependency that leaves the array empty.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_0c7355"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-25T15:45:11.895066+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-25T15:45:25.036952+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:796f2af67e59", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 796f2af67e59 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Never report a worktree-hosted commit as delivered or lost without resolving it from the PARENT repository and checking whether the remote branch contains it as an ancestor. Deleting a temporary worktree removes the checkout, not the commits, because worktrees share the parent object store; but that survival guarantee is worthless if nobody verifies it, so run the reachability check before any temp-directory cleanup and state per-commit push status explicitly.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_796f2a"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-25T15:45:25.036952+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-25T15:45:25.248881+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:5d45449492c4", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 5d45449492c4 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Program-level rows whose names carry a phase prefix and a tasklist pointer are coordination reminders, not implementation lanes. Reconcile them closed against their verified implementation lane with evidence; never claim them for implementation, because the program invariant that created them exists precisely to stop two agents doing the same work under two different ids.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_5d4544"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-25T15:45:25.248881+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-25T15:45:37.207572+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:acd73b8eefbc", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson acd73b8eefbc via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'A queue row can remain claimed by a DEAD agent with no atomic claim row, so stale-claim cleanup has nothing to release and the row strands forever. Close it with a disclosed takeover completion only after independently verifying the work actually landed from current refs, and record the prior agent, its verified DEAD status, and the evidence in the event payload rather than silently reassigning ownership.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_acd73b"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-25T15:45:37.207572+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-25T15:45:37.426944+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:8e8d5636d1c8", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 8e8d5636d1c8 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Stale-claim cleanup can resurrect a task whose retries were already exhausted, because the release path does not consult retry_count before requeueing. After running cleanup, re-read the board and if a retry-exhausted task reappears as queued, re-assert its terminal state explicitly and file the gap as a board-logic caveat instead of leaving a dead task looking claimable.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_8e8d56"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-25T15:45:37.426944+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-25T15:45:37.643259+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:1116a14c3f67", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 1116a14c3f67 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Tasks that require physical hardware execution stay QUEUED with an operator runbook attached; never claim them, never mark them complete, and never substitute synthetic or replayed output for the demanded evidence. Publish the exact command surface, the evidence shape, the sanitization rules, and the completion condition so a human can discharge it without guesswork.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_1116a1"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-25T15:45:37.643259+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-25T15:45:49.530760+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:25db2fe45992", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 25db2fe45992 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Verify a lane claim by re-measuring the exact counts in a CLEAN detached worktree checked out at the claimed commit, not in the primary clone. A primary checkout that has diverged from the upstream branch can produce failures that do not reproduce at the verified ref, so first establish how far the local branch has drifted before attributing any failure to the lane under review.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_25db2f"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-25T15:45:49.530760+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-25T15:45:49.761065+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:56f67143740d", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 56f67143740d via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Treat a board snapshot as a volatile observation, not a source of truth: resolve each task terminal state from its own ordered event timeline before acting. A queue listing read at one moment can show work as open that is already closed, because the board is append-only and busy, so re-read and reconcile per task id rather than reasoning from a single listing.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_56f671"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-25T15:45:49.761065+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-25T15:46:14.574243+00:00", "skill": "agent-coordination-heartbeat", "action": "board-reconciliation", "result": "success", "detail": "success", "pain_score": 2, "importance": 8, "reflection": "Reconciled a 7-row migration reminder batch without claiming any implementation lane: 6 rows closed as superseded against verified lanes with per-row evidence (measured in clean detached worktrees), 1 operator-only row deliberately left queued with a runbook. Cleared a stranded claim held by a verifiably DEAD agent via a disclosed takeover, and caught that stale-claim cleanup had requeued a retry-exhausted task, restoring its terminal state.", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "agent-coordination-heartbeat", "profile": "default", "run_id": "pid-45488", "commit_sha": "101e6526ed8b91b46d1185174665b4841d9fffc6"}, "evidence_ids": ["lesson_5d45449492c4", "lesson_acd73b8eefbc", "lesson_8e8d5636d1c8", "lesson_1116a14c3f67"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-25T15:46:14.673609+00:00", "skill": "shell-hygiene", "action": "clinepass-bash32-nounset-fix", "result": "success", "detail": "success", "pain_score": 2, "importance": 7, "reflection": "Reproduced the dispatch-blocking empty-array nounset abort in the tracked ClinePass wrapper end-to-end with a stubbed CLI, scanned all 128 set -u scripts in the repo to size the blast radius, fixed the single defective file with the length-guard idiom already used by its sibling script, proved the fatal path and the positive path, and committed it on its own branch unpushed.", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "shell-hygiene", "profile": "default", "run_id": "pid-45505", "commit_sha": "101e6526ed8b91b46d1185174665b4841d9fffc6"}, "evidence_ids": ["lesson_0c7355deb939"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-25T15:46:14.774182+00:00", "skill": "codex-dispatch", "action": "deliver-k1-source-provenance-audit", "result": "success", "detail": "success", "pain_score": 2, "importance": 7, "reflection": "Delivered a codex-assigned read-only K1 provenance audit whose assigned Cline worker identity was DEAD with no deliverable: attributed the report to the live identity instead of spoofing a pulse, verified both pinned revisions as real commits, reported per-candidate provenance and the actionable finding that namespace checks are pending on all rows, and kept the audit free of invented owner mappings or copied bodies.", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "codex-dispatch", "profile": "default", "run_id": "pid-45522", "commit_sha": "101e6526ed8b91b46d1185174665b4841d9fffc6"}, "evidence_ids": ["lesson_796f2af67e59", "lesson_25db2fe45992"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-26T05:41:02.058669+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:ad1dc8dc22d7", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson ad1dc8dc22d7 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'When hardening an address or endpoint denylist, add the sibling prefix classes as a set and then verify parity across every layer that dials, because the same class of gap usually exists on more than one side. Concretely: Teredo, 6to4, 6to4 relay anycast, CGNAT, loopback, ULA and link-local travel together, and a fix that lands in only one of the two sibling implementations leaves the other exploitable. Where the two layers sit on opposite sides of a regime boundary, reimplement the rules natively rather than importing across it, and prove parity with matching classification tests on both sides.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_ad1dc8"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-26T05:41:02.058669+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-26T05:41:02.311444+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:4121f37d8f08", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 4121f37d8f08 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'When merging tracked memory across branches, never hand-edit a graduated candidate claim: its id must remain a tooling derivation of that exact claim, so sanitizing or rewording the claim silently invalidates the id and the memory-records gate rejects the commit. Union the JSONL files by id while leaving the target branch rows byte-intact, append only genuinely new rows, then re-render the derived markdown; if a row genuinely needs new text, re-mint it through the memory tooling instead of editing it in place.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_4121f3"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-26T05:41:02.311444+00:00"]}
