{"timestamp": "2026-09-26T07:59:03.424316+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:3c8025df4a77", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 3c8025df4a77 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'When Seth, the GrokBot chief of staff, spawns multiple cloud Cursor agent instances, each instance that writes files uses its own git worktree. A local worker agent liaises between those cloud instances and the MacBook Pro Orchestrator, and the Orchestrator canonical checkout stays put. One agent verifying a claimed commit reads that commit from the canonical checkout and does not create a worktree. Before attributing a failure to the lane under review, judge local-branch divergence with scripts/git/reanchor_scan.sh against origin/main.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_3c8025"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-26T07:59:03.424316+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-26T08:03:00.703421+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:0f93fdb67bc6", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 0f93fdb67bc6 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'A bash script that runs set -u must length-guard EVERY array expansion, because macOS stock bash 3.2 treats an empty-array expansion of the form ${arr[@]} as an unbound-variable error rather than an empty expansion. Canonical idiom: [[ ${#arr[@]} -gt 0 ]] && cmd+=(\"${arr[@]}\"). This is the THIRD recurrence of the same defect class (after commit_clean_test.sh verify_args and a profiling wrapper), so treat it as a systemic pattern: when fixing one instance, scan every set -u script in the repo with a single regex for unguarded += expansions and fix all confirmed instances, then prove the fix against a stubbed dependency that leaves the array empty.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_0f93fd"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-26T08:03:00.703421+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-26T09:25:33.866681+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:3be49392d3d3", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 3be49392d3d3 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'When Seth, the GrokBot chief of staff, spawns multiple cloud Cursor agent instances, each instance that writes files uses its own git worktree. A local worker agent liaises between those cloud instances and the MacBook Pro Orchestrator, and the Orchestrator canonical checkout stays put. One agent verifying a claimed commit reads that commit from the canonical checkout and does not create a worktree. Before attributing a failure to the lane under review, judge local-branch divergence with scripts/git/reanchor_scan.sh . origin/main heads. The heads scope is required because the script defaults to remotes.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_3be493"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-09-26T09:25:33.866681+00:00"]}
