{"timestamp": "2026-10-02T02:32:13.074657+00:00", "skill": "oramasys-method", "action": "containment-hardening", "result": "success", "detail": "success", "pain_score": 5, "importance": 8, "reflection": "Synthesized Cursor and Antigravity containment reviews into paired PT and Orama PR updates. PT now retains direct-child identity until a durable containment annotation, retries transient annotation writes up to three times within one cleanup lifecycle, and reports cli/unresolved when the child remains registered after persistent storage failure. Orama restores approvals only for cli/verified, in-process/not-applicable, or a true legacy response with both fields absent. TestClient deprecation was removed through the supported httpx2 test dependency. Focused verification passed in both repositories. The in-memory jobs-log cache is deliberately deferred to v2 rather than folded into the containment fix.", "confidence": 0.95, "source": {"skill": "oramasys-method", "profile": "default", "run_id": "pid-26771", "commit_sha": "94c65cc099bb1c7a6fec130cc1d91519a175ae76"}, "evidence_ids": []}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-02T04:49:49.010830+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:c55647a2c1fc", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson c55647a2c1fc via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'A self-hosted Cursor worker skips canvas diagnostics when agent-sdk/cursor is absent beside the installed agent build. Point that directory at the SDK shipped in the desktop app agent-exec extension. On a case-insensitive volume, an MCP server directory whose name differs only by case makes stat succeed so the writer skips the update, while the directory listing still reports the configured server id missing; rename the directory to the exact configured id. Cloud plugin install markers that are missing only while the manifest is being written are a race, not a missing plugin, once the marker digest matches the manifest. HTTP/2 PING timeouts and HTTP 504 responses on the worker bridge are session drops; the worker retries, and replacing the process opens a fresh session. Portable memory must not record host names, home paths, process ids, or bridge worker ids.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_c55647"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-02T04:49:49.010830+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-02T04:49:55.392120+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:b8f15928f111", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson b8f15928f111 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Orama pull request 379 changes only the post-merge review sweep workflow and does not change guard-sync files. That workflow is outside the guard-sync manifest, so syncing guard scripts must not copy it into Perpetua-Tools. A clean Perpetua-Tools tree at origin/main is already byte-identical to that pull request for every manifest path, and sync-attribution-guard-scripts.sh from that tree exits without edits. A local checkout that is behind origin/main can report lag even when the published main tree matches; do not treat that lag as a reason to edit guard scripts on a memory branch.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_b8f159"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-02T04:49:55.392120+00:00"]}
