{"timestamp": "2026-10-06T11:09:19.851179+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:466c0e62569c", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 466c0e62569c via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Verify Sites readiness as separate gates: exact assembled bytes, in-memory migrated schema and history query plans, isolated child runtime paths and cancellation cleanup, HTTP status before JSON parsing, owner access, deployment, plugin installation and authenticated MCP calls. A UI error repair is not an OAuth repair; preserve original prompt and memory bytes, retain migration history, and establish rollback before first publication.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_466c0e"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-06T11:09:19.851179+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-06T11:09:20.625420+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:c5a27e219768", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson c5a27e219768 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'A migration verifier must cover the same complete file set and execution order as its applier. Validate index-only boundaries and parse SQL comments and quoted tokens without hiding DML. When a blocked gate later passes, append dated evidence to tracked status before merge; never rewrite the earlier observation or revive retired lesson-rendering targets.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_c5a27e"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-06T11:09:20.625420+00:00"]}
