{"timestamp": "2026-10-09T11:55:11.668386+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:a85daa4f1c2a", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson a85daa4f1c2a via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Extend lesson_9c4f8a7d21be and lesson_c8e4d29b7f31: the approved D-LG-1 split keeps structural GraphSpec, graph_id and structural lint in Core; Oramasys owns an independently hashed graph_id-bound policy and application summary. D-LG-4 Phase 1 permits explicit graph-as-tool and offline agent-as-node bridges, not a framework dependency or production egress. Durable approvals and R3/R4 remain gated.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_a85daa"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-09T11:55:11.668386+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-09T11:55:11.883289+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:cb16bfdcbab7", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson cb16bfdcbab7 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Optional framework compatibility needs Python-native gap errors: ModuleNotFoundError with name for unsupported modules, AttributeError for unsupported attributes, and explicit explain diagnostics when from-import replaces the reason. A finder returning None permits fallthrough; importorskip can hide a real gap. Broken installed transitive imports must propagate, never silently enable fallback.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_cb16bf"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-09T11:55:11.883289+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-09T11:55:12.071672+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:db045b3d50b8", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson db045b3d50b8 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'A passing order test proves input ordering only when completion ordering differs: delay the first async input, keep a serial control, and require the test to kill an as_completed mutant for concurrent limits. Dependency-free exporter stubs prove wiring; separately run pinned real upstream oracles before claiming interoperability.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_db045b"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-09T11:55:12.071672+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-09T11:55:12.264078+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:74321ed18112", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 74321ed18112 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'For coordinated cross-repo publication, preserve historical cutoffs and append current qualifications; link unmerged records to their PR branches, test immutable dependency candidates as explicit overlays, and retain the production pin until merge. Commit logical batches, update each remote branch once with its expected head, and bind review replies and status comments to exact fixing SHAs.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_74321e"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-09T11:55:12.264078+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-09T20:28:30.404515+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:c1b94cabf124", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson c1b94cabf124 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'For a coordinated lockstep change, pin exact peer commit SHAs and contract, fixture, policy and environment digests before testing; update both repositories with implementation, tests, active references and handoff; treat candidate overlays as test-only; and promote a production dependency pin only after upstream merge and downstream full-suite plus oracle revalidation.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_c1b94c"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-09T20:28:30.404515+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-09T23:35:44.879982+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:3eb4165ae12b", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 3eb4165ae12b via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Disjoint file lists do not prove two PRs are independent: merge both into a scratch branch and run the cross-cutting conformance, registry and snapshot tests before reporting no conflict; a planned-field gate fails any code that ships the field early, so flip the registry in the same reviewed step or qualify the registry by profile.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_3eb416"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-09T23:35:44.879982+00:00"]}
