{"timestamp":"2026-09-28T09:14:56.898944+00:00","skill":"audit-integration","action":"evidence-reconstruction:lesson_1bbee93ff11e","result":"verified","detail":"{\"recorded_at\":\"2026-10-12T11:24:45+00:00\",\"kind\":\"historical-provenance-reconstruction\",\"original_evidence_id\":\"2026-09-28T09:14:56.898944+00:00\",\"reason\":\"The original timestamp was absent from preserved live and September 28 archived episodic logs.\",\"verification\":{\"repository\":\"AlphaClaw\",\"worktree\":\"$HOME/code/OpenClaw/AlphaClaw\",\"branch\":\"subagent/mac-orchestrator/alphaclaw-bind-host\",\"commit\":\"55d06572b2ebb9f9a5350eead962ba97db43d6b4\",\"commit_timestamp\":\"2026-09-28T17:10:48+08:00\",\"subject\":\"fix(server): loopback bind on bare metal, 0.0.0.0 in Docker\",\"paths\":[\"lib/platform.js\",\"lib/server/init/server-lifecycle.js\",\"tests/server/platform.test.js\"],\"publication_status\":\"local-only; not contained in main, origin/main, or upstream/main\"},\"disclosure\":\"This additive record was reconstructed during the October 12 audit integration. It is not a recovered contemporaneous runtime event.\"}","pain_score":4,"importance":8,"reflection":"Repaired the lesson evidence link with explicit reconstructed provenance backed by the verified local AlphaClaw implementation.","confidence":0.8,"source":{"skill":"audit-integration","profile":"historical-provenance-remediation","run_id":"pt-memory-audit-20261012","commit_sha":"55d06572b2ebb9f9a5350eead962ba97db43d6b4"},"evidence_ids":["2026-09-28T09:14:56.898944+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-13T03:28:11.766382+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:482aa0d2f685", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 482aa0d2f685 via .agent/tools/learn.py: \"Never call loop.stop() directly from inside an asyncio background task while asyncio.run()'s own top-level future is still pending; signal shutdown via an asyncio.Event and await asyncio.wait({main_task, stop_task}, return_when=FIRST_COMPLETED) instead, then cancel/cleanup gracefully.\"", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_482aa0"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-13T03:28:11.766382+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-13T03:28:22.783594+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:eacd61cbb9c0", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson eacd61cbb9c0 via .agent/tools/learn.py: \"A script shared byte-identically across orama-system and Perpetua-Tools that uses bash-4-only features (mapfile, associative arrays, etc.) silently breaks on any machine whose only bash is macOS's stock 3.2.57 (no GNU bash 4+ installed) -- check 'bash --version' before relying on bash 4 builtins in any shared git hook, and prefer a portable 'while IFS= read -r' loop over mapfile.\"", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_eacd61"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-13T03:28:22.783594+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-13T03:28:36.312037+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:94cbd6e80ee2", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 94cbd6e80ee2 via .agent/tools/learn.py: \"When 'gh'/'git push' auth fails with 'Invalid username or token', check for a stale env var matching the CLI's exact lookup name (GITHUB_TOKEN for gh/git) before assuming the stored credential is broken -- 'gh auth status' with that var unset reveals whether a working keyring-stored token is being shadowed; scope the fix to 'env -u GITHUB_TOKEN <cmd>' per-command rather than editing the secrets file that defines it.\"", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_94cbd6"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-13T03:28:36.312037+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-13T06:44:22.068532+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:f0c0eeafa8ef", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson f0c0eeafa8ef via .agent/tools/learn.py: \"A gate copied from a one-time bootstrap path onto a reconcile-on-every-start path must compare identity, not lifecycle state: state legitimately mutates between starts, so a 'must equal the pristine record' check passes first boot and then refuses every restart after the first write. Before accepting a reviewer-proposed hardening, apply it and run the existing restart tests; and reject guards whose conditions the SELECT or a DB constraint already guarantee, which are false assurance.\"", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_f0c0ee"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-13T06:44:22.068532+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-13T06:44:22.224318+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:ba06d89f1ee2", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson ba06d89f1ee2 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'On Darwin the loser of two concurrent openat(dir_fd, name, O_CREAT) calls on the same new name gets a spurious ENOENT even though the directory exists (absolute paths and Linux are unaffected); retry once without O_CREAT to open what the rival made, keep the ownership and mode checks on the returned descriptor, and cover it with an injected-ENOENT test because Linux CI can never reproduce the race.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_ba06d8"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-13T06:44:22.224318+00:00"]}
