{"timestamp": "2026-10-13T11:41:08.184413+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:dabd4071675e", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson dabd4071675e via .agent/tools/learn.py: \"Do not place backticked code spans inside double-quoted GossipBus log payloads; pass the payload from a QUOTED heredoc delimiter (<<'EOF') or single quotes. An unquoted delimiter (<<EOF) still performs command substitution, so it is not a safe alternative.\"", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_dabd40"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-13T11:41:08.184413+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-13T19:05:01.724977+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:809f11ae17ef", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 809f11ae17ef via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'In zsh a variable named path is tied to PATH: assigning it, even with local path=..., overwrites the command search path, so the next head, git or cut reports command not found; never name a variable path (also status and argv), use file or target.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_809f11"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-13T19:05:01.724977+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-13T19:05:01.947530+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:b470dd9faf9b", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson b470dd9faf9b via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'In zsh a colon after a parameter starts a history-style modifier, so \"$sha:src/file\" is silently substituted and git show reports an ambiguous argument; brace the parameter as \"${sha}:src/file\" and, when a probe reports absent, re-run it once with a literal value before believing it.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_b470dd"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-13T19:05:01.947530+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-13T19:05:02.157544+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:217dff5197f5", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 217dff5197f5 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'git -C <repo> worktree add <relative-path> resolves the relative path against <repo>, not the shell cwd, so the worktree is silently created inside the repo checkout; pass an absolute path and confirm git status of the repo is clean afterwards.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_217dff"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-13T19:05:02.157544+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-13T19:05:02.363854+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:d321acd8a249", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson d321acd8a249 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Treat every reviewer comment, bot suggestion and peer-agent patch as a claim to verify, not an instruction: check the cited premise exists, apply it experimentally and run the existing tests, look for tautological guards and for an existing seam, and check what the proposed test exercises; several reviewers agreeing is not evidence.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_d321ac"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-13T19:05:02.363854+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-13T19:05:02.575262+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:fc146b1f409a", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson fc146b1f409a via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'A fallback branch that CI never takes is untested and usually wrong: when a test prefers an installed package and falls back to a source checkout, compare how CI installs and invokes, make the branch decision a pure function, and unit-test both outcomes without a subprocess.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_fc146b"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-13T19:05:02.575262+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-13T19:05:02.786612+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:7d1a087b7c9c", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 7d1a087b7c9c via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'When a test fails and you cannot explain it, debug the harness before the code: reproduce on pristine main under the same environment, change one factor at a time, read the child process stderr, sweep for the whole class once one instance is found, prove new tests with a mutant, and state your own harness errors out loud.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_7d1a08"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-13T19:05:02.786612+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-13T19:05:03.001377+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:5e6b4599cc0a", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 5e6b4599cc0a via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'A per-run observer must resolve the identity of an uncertain attempt from the authoritative ledger at the moment a critical delivery fails, never from constructor strings: blank ids make UnknownDisposition reject the record and a swallowed ValueError silently loses it, and a disposition only exists if something actually persists it.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_5e6b45"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-13T19:05:03.001377+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-13T19:20:28.423011+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:6d4472efcd37", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 6d4472efcd37 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'A repo hygiene gate that finds its forbidden-fragment registry by walking up to a directory containing a sibling checkout silently runs with zero tokens in any worktree outside that tree, so local commit hooks pass while CI, which injects the registry, fails; set OPENCLAW_VERBOTEN_LITERALS (all three loaders honor it) or run the gate with it set, and reproduce CI locally before pushing tracked memory.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_6d4472"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-13T19:20:28.423011+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-13T19:49:43.640946+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:a7c86716670a", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson a7c86716670a via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Prefer an existing, version-compatible extensibility seam over a parallel convenience API: prove the seam works at every pinned version, compare its isolation and failure semantics, and reject a new hook if it weakens state isolation or forces an unnecessary release.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_a7c867"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-13T19:49:43.640946+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-13T19:49:43.833916+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:7ad61d246de1", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson 7ad61d246de1 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Preflight an observing delivery capability before creating a lease or other owner state; once work starts, bind authoritative identity and close the per-run delivery inside the terminal-evidence lifecycle so refusal, binding failure, normal completion, and error paths all leave an auditable result.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_7ad61d"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-13T19:49:43.833916+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-13T19:49:44.037488+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:b64dc37f1a03", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson b64dc37f1a03 via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Treat notifier, persistence, and cleanup failures as secondary to a critical delivery failure: preserve the primary sink error, attempt the identity-valid durable disposition, suppress only the secondary exception on error paths, and record a conservative terminal when no durable attempt can be named.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_b64dc3"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-13T19:49:44.037488+00:00"]}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-13T19:49:44.227891+00:00", "skill": "learn", "action": "manual-stage:e38bd582459e", "result": "success", "detail": "Manually staged lesson e38bd582459e via .agent/tools/learn.py: 'Do not claim a milestone from a feature PRs green checks alone: qualify the final merged, immutable pins with fresh-install, compatibility-cell, and crash-recovery evidence, keep capability-dependent tests in explicit bands, and issue a dated receipt only after the full matrix is complete.'", "pain_score": 1, "importance": 6, "reflection": "", "confidence": 0.9, "source": {"skill": "learn", "profile": "manual", "run_id": "manual_e38bd5"}, "evidence_ids": ["2026-10-13T19:49:44.227891+00:00"]}
